=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
A complete four-phase diagnostic pass found no fault in this topology. Phase 1 reachability showed 0% loss across all host-to-server paths. Phase A (infra_sweep + l2_snapshot) found no ACL rules, no addressing anomalies, no real MAC conflicts — the "duplicate MACs" flagged by l2_snapshot are null-MAC Linux kernel tunnel pseudo-interfaces (tunl0, gre0, etc.) that are DOWN on every device, a normal artifact. Phase B confirmed the OSPF fabric is fully converged across all six FRR routers with all adjacencies in Full state, and tc_snapshot found only the default pfifo_fast qdisc on every inspected interface — no traffic shaping or injected latency anywhere. Phase D (service_snapshot + pressure_sweep) confirmed that both hosts resolve all four web hostnames (web0–3.local) to the correct IPs via dns_server (10.200.0.2) and receive HTTP 200 responses in ~3 ms; dns_server itself is under zero CPU or socket pressure.

The user's report describes intermittent DNS slowness ("sometimes instantly, sometimes spinning"). The mechanism that would produce this — a tc-injected delay on dns_server's egress, a resource-exhaustion script, a link flap script, or a daemon crash-restart loop — is absent. There is no flap process, no carrier history, no syslog evidence, and no tc rule present. The current state is fully healthy with no trace of a past transient. The claim is unconfirmed.

Root cause: no fault is present; the reported intermittent behavior has no observable mechanism or historical trace in the live topology.

Fix: no corrective action required. If the symptom recurs, capture a concurrent `nslookup` timing and `dns_client_snapshot` run during the slow period to confirm whether the delay is resolver-side or network-path-side.
=== END ===